From: Hans Christian Winther-Sorensen <hc@wsh.no>
Subject: [PATCH] esp: treat a selection timeout as no device at that target

Since 56fa1b2a72 ("esp: use ESP rather than DMA interrupt to detect end
of transfer") and c3a19c1e54 ("esp: correctly terminate successful SCSI
commands"), do_command() only returns non-zero when the status register
lacks ESP_STAT_TCNT. A selection timeout on an empty target raises
ESP_INTR_DC with a status of 0, so do_command() returned 0 (success) and
inquiry() marked every empty target present, with an "UNKNOWN" media type
read from the IDENTIFY byte left in the buffer.

ob_esp_init() then numbered the empty targets 0-2 before the disk on
target 3: the disk got only the aliases disk3/hd3, there was no disk alias
any more, and the default boot-device "disk:a disk" (SPARCstation 5, disk
on SCSI target 3) failed with "No valid state has been set by load or
init-program".

Return an error when the selection ends in a disconnect.
---
diff --git a/drivers/esp.c b/drivers/esp.c
index 92f28cc..bd1a497 100644
--- a/drivers/esp.c
+++ b/drivers/esp.c
@@ -86,7 +86,7 @@ static void dump_drive(sd_private_t *drive)
 static int
 do_command(esp_private_t *esp, sd_private_t *sd, int cmdlen, int replylen)
 {
-    int status;
+    int status, intr;
 
     // Set SCSI target
     esp->ll->regs[ESP_BUSID] = sd->id & 7;
@@ -104,10 +104,16 @@ do_command(esp_private_t *esp, sd_private_t *sd, int cmdlen, int replylen)
     // Set ATN, issue command
     esp->ll->regs[ESP_CMD] = ESP_CMD_SELA | ESP_CMD_DMA;
     // Wait for ESP to complete
-    while (!(esp->ll->regs[ESP_INTRPT] & (ESP_INTR_BSERV | ESP_INTR_FDONE | ESP_INTR_DC)));
+    while (!((intr = esp->ll->regs[ESP_INTRPT]) & (ESP_INTR_BSERV | ESP_INTR_FDONE | ESP_INTR_DC)));
     // Check status
     status = esp->ll->regs[ESP_STATUS];
 
+    /* Selection timed out: there is no device at this target */
+    if (intr & ESP_INTR_DC) {
+        DPRINTF("do_command: id %d, selection timeout\n", sd->id);
+        return -1;
+    }
+
     DPRINTF("do_command: id %d, cmd[0] 0x%x, status 0x%x\n", sd->id, esp->buffer[1], status);
 
     /* Target didn't want all command data? */
